# The build venv's tooling, as this repository chooses it (ticket 25).
#
# Compiled to wheelbuild/requirements.txt, which is what the build installs;
# regenerate with the command in that file's header after editing this one.
#
# What is deliberately NOT here: the three requirements that come out of the
# drivers at run time, so that each stays pinned in one place — nanobind
# (wheelbuild.dolfinx.NANOBIND_REQUIREMENT), the upstream trio (read from this
# project's own pyproject.toml), and the `mpich` bound (derived from
# wheelbuild.mpich.MPICH_VERSION). A copy of any of them here would be a
# second pin to keep in step. Their own transitive dependencies come with them
# and are not locked here either — fenics-ffcx brings cffi, for one — which is
# the recorded limit of this file: it pins the tooling this repository chose,
# not the closure of three requirements it deliberately reads from elsewhere.

# Packaging drivers.
build
wheel
setuptools
packaging

# What decides what the published wheel claims: auditwheel rewrites sonames
# and grafts libraries into the payload, and abi3audit --strict is the only
# thing standing behind the abi3 tag.
auditwheel
abi3audit

# Compiled against: petsc4py's and slepc4py's extensions are built against
# these numpy headers, and the import check runs against this mpi4py.
numpy>=2
mpi4py

# What petsc4py's and slepc4py's setup.py need, and what DOLFINx's own
# bindings are configured by.
cython>=3
scikit-build-core>=0.11

# Pinned for the same reason as the rest: it is what resolves everything
# above, and `pip install --upgrade pip` is a different pip every month.
pip
